   141	### 4.2 Oracles
   142	
   143	**Rule: every case names an oracle that imports no production visibility, constraint, projection, hydration
   144	or codec code.** The KV runtime (O-KV) runs as a regression participant only and never closes anything alone
   145	(review r1 finding 5).
   146	
   147	| Oracle | Status | What it is |
   148	| --- | --- | --- |
   149	| O-EVT | EXISTS | `qualification/workloads/event_oracles.py`, packet answers from immutable events |
   150	| O-REPLAY | TO-BUILD | new independent Python event-replay oracle, specified below |
   151	| O-HAM | EXISTS | finite-nine historical assertion metadata oracle (v1, v2) |
   152	| O-CFG8 | EXISTS | configured-eight fixture oracle |
   153	| O-STR, O-COLL | EXISTS | frozen codepoint-order arrays (string-order-v1, collation tiny control) |
   154	| O-SHAPE | TO-AUTHOR | frozen expected answers for negation and aggregate edge shapes |
   155	| O-ERR | TO-AUTHOR | frozen expected typed error per negative case |
   156	| O-TESTKIT | EXISTS | authored expectations inside the unchanged44 cases |
   157	| O-OBS | TO-AUTHOR | observation protocol for cancellation, drain, connections, lifecycle |
   158	| O-SPEC | TO-AUTHOR | TypeScript type witnesses against packed declarations |
   159	| O-KV | EXISTS | KV runtime, regression participant only |
   160	
   161	**Oracle lifecycle.** TO-BUILD or TO-AUTHOR, then BUILT, then ACCEPTED after an independent review recorded in
   162	the commit. Only an ACCEPTED oracle, with its file hashes pinned in the contract version, can close an
   163	obligation.
   164	
   165	**What O-REPLAY must compute** (the later oracle experiment builds it; this is its specification):
   166	
   167	1. **Inputs.** The command stream (ordered commands with operations, typed values in canonical encoding,
   168	   entity ids and types, valid intervals, preconditions, meta: actor, commandId, correlationId, causationId,
   169	   configSnapshot), enforcement mode and constraint rules, schema releases, and the ACK receipts from the
   170	   system under test. Receipts are the only system-provided input: outcome, txId, position, instant and the
   171	   assertion ids assigned per operation.
   172	2. **Receipt consistency.** Positions dense and increasing per scope, instants non-decreasing in position order,
   173	   ids unique, rejected commands hold no position. An inconsistent receipt fails the run.
   174	3. **Expected command outcomes.** Committed, or the expected typed failure: CommandAlreadyCommitted with the
   175	   original txId, TransactionConflict, Required, Cardinality, Unique and ReferenceTarget violations, reserved
   176	   namespace, invalid value.
   177	4. **Assertion relation with complete metadata.** id, entityId, attribute, exact typed value (int64 as a Python
   178	   int, binary64 as IEEE bits, text as a codepoint sequence, datetime, ref, json in canonical and original key
   179	   order, blob descriptor), validFrom, validTo, recordedAt, recordedPosition, createdBy, entityType,
   180	   schemaVersion, txId, retractedAt, retractedPosition, retractTxId.
   181	5. **Visibility at a cut** (scope, P, optional R, V): recorded-visible and not retracted at the cut, valid at V
   182	   under half-open `[validFrom, validTo)`.
   183	6. **Both history contracts.** Raw lifetime (complete retirement fields) and as-of snapshot (retirement fields
   184	   null unless `retractedPosition <= P` and, when R is bound, `retractedAt <= R`).
   185	7. **Entity models.** Per EntityType at a basis: cardinality-one value or the conflict outcome, cardinality-many
   186	   arrays in the specified order, absent optional as a missing property, includes resolved at the same basis,
   187	   timelines.
   188	8. **Transactions.** Records per position with meta fields and changes in write order.
   189	9. **Cursors.** Expected page sequences at a fixed basis for a declared order key and page size.
   190	10. **Supports.** Live support counts per value and per derived fact, reachability supports for DAG cases.
   191	11. **Arithmetic and order.** Exact int64 with overflow detection, IEEE binary64, codepoint string order. No
   192	    casefolding.
   193	12. **Analytic scale counts.** Population counts for the scale generator without materializing the dataset.
   194	13. **Self-checks before ACCEPTED.** Reproduce the O-HAM finite-nine and O-CFG8 tiny-v4 expectations, and the
   195	    O-EVT cut semantics on the packet events where the domains overlap; unit tests for every rule above.
   196	
   197	Decisions the oracle needs and nobody has made yet are listed as open questions in the report (conflict rule
   198	for equal duplicates, card-many order, partial-sum overflow, AVG type, division by zero).
