   200	### 4.3 Mutation controls
   201	
   202	**A suite that cannot fail proves nothing.** Each mutant is applied only to the system under test (build flag or
   203	patch, its hash recorded), never to an oracle or case file. CR-MUTANT-KILL requires at least one FAIL per mutant
   204	on the same candidate tree.
   205	
   206	| Mutant | Fault it injects |
   207	| --- | --- |
   208	| M-HALF-OPEN | validTo inclusive or validFrom exclusive |
   209	| M-DROPPED-SUPPORT | retracting one of two supports removes the value |
   210	| M-FUTURE-RETIREMENT | snapshot reads leak retirements recorded after the cut |
   211	| M-INT64-ROUND | int64 passes through binary64 |
   212	| M-ENTITY-TYPE-SWAP | two EntityType labels swapped |
   213	| M-STALE-PROJECTION | projection one publication behind while reporting the latest basis |
   214	| M-CUT-OFF-BY-ONE | P-1, or R treated as exclusive |
   215	| M-NEGZERO | -0.0 becomes +0.0 |
   216	| M-ICU-ORDER | locale collation instead of codepoint order |
   217	| M-SCOPE-LEAK | scope predicate dropped on one path |
   218	| M-MASK-RAW | snapshot mask applied to the raw lifetime contract |
   219	| M-CONFLICT-PICK | card-one conflict resolved by arbitrary pick |
   220	| M-IDENTITY-COLLAPSE | same-value assertions in one batch share one id |
   221	| M-JOURNAL-ORDER | transaction changes reordered |
   222	| M-CLAIM-IGNORED | duplicate command commits twice |
   223	| M-DECORRELATE | negation helper omits correlated re-binding |
   224	| M-STALE-REUSE | reused result not invalidated |
   225	| M-CARD-MANY-DROP | one card-many element dropped |
   226	
   227	The first six are the ones the brief requires; all eighteen are killed by `R.repo.mutation-controls`, and each
   228	is also attached to the obligations it most directly protects.
