   253	### 5.2 Closure rules
   254	
   255	| Rule | Holds when |
   256	| --- | --- |
   257	| CR-PASS-ALL | every declared case runs in every declared mode, each result PASS against the named oracle, executed ids equal the declared set |
   258	| CR-COUNTEREXAMPLE | the original counterexample runs with its original frozen expected answer (oracle hash unchanged since the first recorded failure) and passes; the raw counterexample text is unedited |
   259	| CR-MUTANT-KILL | each listed mutant, on the same tree, makes at least one case FAIL; the unmutated suite passes |
   260	| CR-OBSERVE | every required O-OBS level is evidenced and joined to one request or connection identity within the stated bounds; uncertainty fails |
   261	| CR-FAULT | every fault point injected the stated number of times (3 unless stated); post-state equals O-REPLAY through every listed access path; zero ACKed commands lost; zero unresolved outcomes |
   262	| CR-STATIC | positive witnesses compile, negative witnesses fail with the expected diagnostic, against packed declarations |
   263	| CR-SCALE | dataset counts verified by independent count queries and O-REPLAY analytic counts; capacity-admitted; correctness subsample passes with zero tolerance |
   264	| CR-PERF | each named CALIBRATE threshold frozen in a calibration receipt that predates acceptance; three independent runs all meet it |
   265	| CR-METRICS | every listed metric present, measured, bound to dataset and build identity |
   266	| CR-LOAD | `load-contract.json` at its frozen version: calibration predates; every invariant and threshold met in each required run |
   267	| CR-MATRIX | every capability cell with a non-empty required-by list is EXACT with a passing receipt; KNOWN-LIMIT cells have empty required-by, a retained counterexample receipt and a raw-guide entry |
   268	| CR-PROVENANCE | the raw recipes' authoring manifest lists only the raw-query guide and engine docs as inputs, and the author differs from the lane's repository and projection authors |
