   274	### 5.3 Goal status algorithm
   275	
   276	```
   277	for each lane L, candidate tree T:
   278	  for each obligation O with L in O.lanes:
   279	      key  = L if O.receiptScope == "lane" else engineOfLane[L]
   280	      R    = acceptance receipts for (O.id, key) that pass V1..V16 on T (or carry forward, 5.5)
   281	      closed(O, L, T) = R non-empty  and  every rule in O.closure.rules holds over R
   282	                        and O.grounding != "policy-pending"
   283	  for each section S: closed(S, L, T) = all closed(O, L, T) for O with S in O.goals
   284	done(T) = all sections closed for all lanes  and  integrated verification receipt (5.6)
   285	```
   286	
   287	A `policy-pending` obligation keeps its section OPEN until a later contract version freezes the policy and
   288	replaces the obligation's statement with the policy's cases.
   289	
   290	### 5.4 Loophole bans
   291	
   292	Each of these is a way a goal could look closed while the system does not meet it. Each is banned, and the
   293	validity rule or closure rule that enforces the ban is named.
   294	
   295	| # | Loophole | Ban | Enforced by |
   296	| --- | --- | --- | --- |
