   298	| B2 | **Unsupported markers.** "unsupported", "not implemented", a capability flag set to false, or a typed refusal of a shape the obligation requires. | Counts as FAIL. Refusing a required shape never closes an obligation, even when the refusal is correct and typed. | V10, R.native.fragment-equivalence, CR-MATRIX |
   299	| B3 | **Lowered thresholds.** A CALIBRATE value set or later changed to make a run pass. | Thresholds are frozen in a create-only calibration receipt before acceptance, respect the hard floors and ceilings in `load-contract.json`, and may only be tightened. A changed profile is a new named profile; the original remains the acceptance profile and its failures stay. | CR-PERF, CR-LOAD, L.calibration.frozen |
   300	| B4 | **Stale builds.** Typecheck of new source while executing old `dist`, or a dirty tree identified only by a dirty flag. | The receipt binds the full tree including uncommitted changes and the hashes of the `dist` files actually imported, built in the same run. | V2, V3 |
   301	| B5 | **Wrong endpoints.** A run against the homebase (15442, 17019), another slot, or an engine started from a different image. | The contacted endpoint must equal the slot's; the image digest must equal the pin. | V5, V6 |
   302	| B6 | **Hybrid-language tasks counted for one language.** A task whose driver is SQL and final read XTQL counted as XTQL. | A hybrid task counts for neither XTDB language; host steps that touch data make a task hybrid. | V11, PKT.full142 |
   303	| B7 | **Calibration runs as acceptance.** | `runKind` must be `acceptance`; calibration, diagnostic, probe and author-preview runs close nothing. | V12 |
   304	| B8 | **Inherited homebase receipts.** Anything in `qualification/reviews`, `.devloop`, the handoff, or another machine. | Only receipts produced by `lab/bin` in this repository count. Section 9 is reference only. | V1 |
   305	| B9 | **Oracle or expected-answer edits.** Rewriting an oracle, casefolding, re-sorting a returned page, or filtering engine output to manufacture a pass. | Oracle and case files are hash-pinned per contract version; a change after a first failure is a new case version and the original stays required; every change needs a verifier review recorded in the commit. | V7, CR-COUNTEREXAMPLE |
